<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="nanoMIPS:LE:32:default:default">
<!--
    Kuna #1631: nanoMIPS had no SLEIGH language, so nanoMIPS code could not be
    loaded at all ("No sleigh specification for nanoMIPS:LE:32:default").

    The image is `nanomips-elf-gcc -O2` (MediaTek GNU Tools 2021.11-07, GCC
    6.3.0) output for

        int ext(int a, int b) { return (a ^ b) + (b << 3); }
        int sum(const int *p, int n) { int s = 0; for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) s += p[i]; return s; }
        int wrap(int a, int b) { int r = ext(a + 1, b * 3); return ext(r, a) + b; }
        int sel(int x) { switch (x) { case 0: return 11; case 1: return 22; case 2: return 37;
                                      case 3: return 41; case 4: return 5; default: return ext(x, x); } }
        unsigned big(unsigned x) { return x * 3 + 0x12345678; }

    linked at 0x1000 with .rodata (the five-byte switch table) directly behind
    .text. It covers the three instruction lengths (16-bit `xor`, 32-bit `lsa`,
    48-bit `addiu`), SAVE / RESTORE.JRC, MOVEP, MOVE.BALC, the scaled indexed
    load LWXS, the PC-relative LAPC and the BRSC table jump.

    Stage: 02 P-code lift (new SLEIGH language) + P0 compiler spec (p32 ABI).
    No option: a language that decodes is not a judgement call. Before this
    change the image does not load; the asserts pin the lifted output.
-->
